// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CUNEIFORM TABLET — a reed stylus impresses wedge-signs into wet clay, sign by
// sign, down ruled cases. Each wedge is a triangular depression that catches a
// raking lamp: as the light rakes across the tablet the whole relief field
// shimmers, far rims glinting and near rims falling to shadow. When the tablet
// is full it dries and a fresh damp tablet is set down (reseed) — a perpetual
// scribe's desk. Warm clay, fired terracotta, grey diorite stone, or lapis
// picked out in cold light.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

